## Context

Roar step 6 for PR #1211 (ImperialDragonHarness, 2026-10-05): the
review-attribution record could not be captured. The writer line requires
the verbatim provider-qualified model id; on the Mistral Vibe runtime the
session cannot learn it. Probed: ~/.vibe/config.toml (no model key),
session logs under ~/.vibe/logs/session/unified/<id>/ (provider masked as
"configured", session_metadata.active_model null, provider_operations carry
no model field), environment (nothing). The attribution contract
(docs/2026-10-02-reviewer-attribution-design.md §4) forbids reconstructing
an id from an alias, and scripts/attribution_record.py correctly refuses
placeholders ("model must be the verbatim provider-qualified id").

Consequence: every reviewed PR wrapped up from this runtime is a capture
failure for the 1004/1005 attribution program — the reviewer seats
(agent.spawn takes no model pin either) and the writer are both
unnameable at the model level. First observed on PR #1211; draft
preserved at memory/pending-capture-pr1211.md.txt on branch
roar/0887-activation-wrapup.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A session running on the Vibe runtime can obtain its verbatim
      provider-qualified model id (and per-seat ids for spawned subagents)
      through a sanctioned, durable source: a CLI flag, an environment
      variable, or a field in the session logs that today masks it as
      "configured" — or the attribution contract and validator gain an
      explicitly modeled "runtime-masked" fact that keeps re-audition
      honestly impossible rather than silently wrong.
- [ ] The PR #1211 attribution record is captured from the then-available
      facts, or the pending capture is explicitly resolved as impossible.

## Invariants
- No reconstruction of model ids from aliases or third-party notes.
- The validator keeps refusing free-text placeholders.

## Raid Imagine (2026-10-06)
Explicit author selection: 1038 first, then1032. Original exits/invariants unchanged. Installed Vibe logger exposes a configured alias or routed default, not historical verbatim provider identities. Choose explicitly typed runtime-masked writer/reviewer facts with required durable evidence and no model/model-version. Keep rejecting placeholders. Exclude whole masked games from model estimates and correlation, report masks visibly in counts and range coverage. Preserve original PR1211 pending draft and append resolution; capture its15actual attempts, with documented blocker-to-verifiable normalization. No historical-unavailable state is introduced here. About10content paths; no package/library search is useful for this fixed existing parser contract. Upstream exposure alone cannot recover historical1211; typed facts require bounded implementation, no author work or provider expense.
BLIND-SPOT: Existing1009 requires actual records for every reviewed merge. PR1204 historical writer unavailable is distinct from runtime masking; prose impossibility alone cannot authorize parent closure. Preserve that limit for1032.

